course: dictionary
lesson: 6337
title: Mourn: deep sadness and loss
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mourn is a verb. To mourn is to feel and show deep sadness because someone has died. In «Jewish families «sit shiva», a week of mourning at home», the word mourning names the sad time a family spends after a death.
explain: Mourn can also mean to feel sad that something is gone or lost. «We mourned the end of the holidays» does not mean anyone died. It means we felt sad that the fun was over. The clue is the word holidays: something good had ended.
explain: To work out which meaning fits, ask: has someone died, or has something gone? Look for phrases too: mourn the death of, mourn for, in mourning, a period of mourning.
fact: Mourn is a verb. Its forms are mourn, mourns, mourned and mourning.
fact: «Mourn» means to feel and show deep sadness because someone has died.
fact: «Mourning» can mean a time of sadness after a death, as in «a period of mourning».
fact: «Sit shiva» is a week of mourning at home, when friends visit with food and comfort.
fact: The sentence «Christians believe God comforts all who mourn» shows that people who mourn can receive comfort.
exercise: «Christians believe God comforts all who mourn.» What does mourn mean here? | To laugh loudly at a party | *To feel deep sadness because someone has died | To run very fast | To count money carefully
exercise: «We mourned the end of the holidays.» Did someone die here? | Yes, a relative had died | No, we were very cross and shouted | Yes, the family moved away for ever | *No, we were sad that something good was over
exercise: In the sentence about sitting shiva, what is the mourning? | A new shop opening on the high street | A school trip to the seaside | A party with games and music | *A week of sadness at home after a death
test:
«A Christian funeral comforts those who mourn.» What does mourn mean? | *To feel deep sadness because someone has died | To cook a big dinner for friends | To paint a picture of the sea | To win a race
test:
Which phrase means a time of sadness after someone has died? | To mourn for a day | *A period of mourning | A period of sunshine | To mourn in a park
exam:
In «Christians believe God comforts all who mourn», what does mourn mean, and which clue helps you know? | *Feel deep sadness because someone has died, and the word comforts | Feel cold, and the word sunny | Feel tired, and the word race | Feel proud, and the word prize
